      "title": "Figma trains specialized editing model for design workflows",
      "summary": "Figma shared research on training a specialized AI model tailored for design editing workflows. The company demonstrated that focused post-training can rival frontier models when executing multi-step manipulations directly on design canvases.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Figma applies specialized post-training to design editing workflows.",
        "Tailored models aim to match frontier model editing performance.",
        "Research focuses on native canvas manipulations rather than external code."
      ],
      "design_implication": "When an agent attempts to edit nested components on a canvas, general frontier models frequently break auto-layout and component hierarchy. With models post-trained directly on canvas operations, design agents interpret spatial structures and property overrides natively rather than guessing through abstracted code. Start auditing library component constraints and naming conventions today, ensuring automated canvas manipulations respect layout rules during complex handoffs.",
      "implication_lens": "capability",
      "visual_need": "illustrate",
