      "title": "Google Gemini adds inline preview and editing for office files",
      "summary": "Google launched native file generation, previewing, and editing within Gemini chats for all users. The capability supports Google Docs, Sheets, slide decks, PDFs, Markdown, and code on the web, with PDF support also available on mobile.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Available immediately to all Gemini users on the web.",
        "Supports Google Docs, Sheets, slides, PDFs, Markdown, and code.",
        "Mobile editing and previewing is currently limited to PDFs."
      ],
      "design_implication": "When an assistant produces structured deliverables like reports or data sheets, forcing users into external applications shatters task momentum. Embedding bi-directional document editors directly inside chat turns ephemeral text responses into durable collaborative artifacts where users refine layouts and copy in place. Start replacing static text summaries and download links in chat flows with embedded, editable surface containers.",
      "implication_lens": "pattern",
      "visual_need": "illustrate",
      "source_name": "The Verge (AI)",
      "source_url": "https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1022519/google-gemini-file-editing-documents-pdfs",
      "source_date": "2026-10-29",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "claim": "Gemini now supports generating, previewing, and editing multiple file formats directly inside chat.",
          "quote": "Now you can generate, preview, and edit PDFs, Google Docs, Google Sheets, slide decks, Markdown files, TXT files, and code directly within Google Gemini."
        },
        {
          "claim": "The feature is live for all Gemini users, with web support for all formats and mobile limited to PDFs.",
          "quote": "The new file editing capabilities are available starting today for all Gemini users, and while PDF previews/editing works on both the web and mobile, all other file formats are only in the web version for now."
        }
